# Best Pattern for Using Flip with React

Based on the forum discussion, the recommended approach involves two key techniques:

## Capturing State Before React Commits

The critical insight is timing: "when the `expand` updates and the component re-renders, when it reaches this line, the old DOM still exists! And the new DOM has not yet been mounted."

Capture the Flip state **during render** (before the DOM updates), then apply the animation in `useLayoutEffect`:

```javascript
const state = Flip.getState(".box"); // Capture before DOM commits
useLayoutEffect(() => {
  if (!state) return;
  Flip.from(state);
}, [expand]);
```

## Recommended: Use useGSAP Hook

The official recommendation from Rodrigo (GSAP administrator) is to use the `useGSAP` hook for better scoping and cleanup:

```javascript
useGSAP(() => {
  state && Flip.from(state, config);
}, {
  dependencies: [expand],
});
```

**Key advantage:** The `useGSAP` hook provides automatic cleanup and prevents memory leaks in your React application, making it the preferred pattern over raw `useLayoutEffect`.

input.codeSketch:
```tsx
"use client";
import { useState, useLayoutEffect, useRef } from "react";
import { gsap } from "gsap";
import { Flip } from "gsap/Flip";
gsap.registerPlugin(Flip);

export function StoryGrid({ stories }: { stories: Story[] }) {
  const [tag, setTag] = useState<string | null>(null);
  const flipState = useRef<Flip.FlipState | null>(null);

  const visible = tag ? stories.filter(s => s.tags.includes(tag)) : stories;

  const onTagClick = (next: string | null) => {
    const reduce = window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
    if (!reduce) {
      // Capture BEFORE setState — old DOM is still mounted right now
      flipState.current = Flip.getState(".story-card", { props: "opacity" });
    }
    setTag(next);
  };

  useLayoutEffect(() => {
    if (!flipState.current) return;
    Flip.from(flipState.current, {
      duration: 0.6,
      ease: "power2.inOut",
      absolute: true,            // pin cards during tween — grid won't fight inversions
      stagger: 0.02,
      onEnter: el => gsap.fromTo(el, { opacity: 0, scale: 0.9 }, { opacity: 1, scale: 1, duration: 0.4 }),
      onLeave: el => gsap.to(el, { opacity: 0, scale: 0.9, duration: 0.3 }),
    });
    flipState.current = null;
  }, [tag]);

  return (
    <>
      <TagBar onSelect={onTagClick} />
      <div className="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        {visible.map(s => (
          <article key={s.id} data-flip-id={s.id} className="story-card">{s.title}</article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </>
  );
}
```
